449],[679,185],[874,992],[764,102],[259,116],[497,480],[323,585],[686,842],[665,769],[736,833],[278,489],[773,844],[837,954],[509,488],[206,954],[46,867],[577,130],[670,890],[992,871],[90,863],[375,513],[901,831],[294,514],[613,755],[143,826],[359,696],[429,423],[949,867],[643,523],[789,953],[254,824],[309,876],[856,826],[801,507],[188,820],[802,94],[553,476],[228,124],[253,955],[769,511],[633,438],[368,633],[483,722],[380,638],[371,354],[696,851],[283,874],[401,867],[389,857],[309,509],[252,551],[488,715],[555,461],[125,907],[295,867],[57,917],[1023,1006],[755,785],[93,948],[947,949],[310,519],[366,519],[179,206],[519,882],[514,902],[765,784],[0,1007],[732,323],[327,424],[835,914],[731,416],[730,449],[483,705],[239,915],[866,161],[208,914],[804,915],[545,481],[399,860],[399,413],[53,834],[979,922],[845,171],[735,790],[556,907],[264,622],[900,794],[744,790],[909,916],[696,582],[983,837],[203,210],[602,235],[871,792],[745,874],[693,606],[492,702],[141,791],[442,544],[169,788],[660,434],[777,853],[662,404],[758,864],[811,969],[585,735],[519,790],[394,431],[317,438],[664,451],[739,462]]}},"text":{"2":"One crisp autumn morning, the trees on Maple Street turned orange, red, and gold. Leaves twirled down like tiny dancers. Jodie raked them into the biggest pile in the whole wide world. Then she jumped right in. CRUNCH! \u201cBodie!\u201d she called. \u201cCome and jump!\u201d","14":"Jodie found a pumpkin that was just right, round and not too heavy. And Waffles? Waffles found the tiniest pumpkin in the whole patch. He carried it in his mouth, very carefully and very proudly, like a treasure.","20":"Next, they drew faces with a marker. Jodie drew a big silly face with three teeth and one wink. Bodie drew a shy smile, just like his own. Then they drew a face on Waffles\u2019 tiny pumpkin too: two floppy ears and a happy tongue.","46":"At last, it was Halloween! Jodie zipped into her witch dress. Bodie climbed into his pumpkin. They stood side by side in front of Jodie\u2019s house. \u201cWe look AMAZING,\u201d said Jodie. Waffles barked and wagged so hard that his whole body wiggled.","50":"Suddenly, something went flap-flap-flap across the big round moon. Bodie grabbed Jodie\u2019s arm. \u201cWhat\u2019s THAT?\u201d Jodie\u2019s mom smiled. \u201cThose are bats. They come out at night to eat bugs. They\u2019re the moon\u2019s little helpers.\u201d One bat did a loop. Bodie gave it a little wave."}}